==================================================
ANALYSIS
==================================================

The web build successfully:
1. Serves all 4 artifacts (HTML, JS, WASM, data) via HTTP
2. Loads and executes the Emscripten JS glue code
3. Downloads and instantiates the 62MB WASM module
4. Initializes IDBFS persistent storage via IndexedDB
5. Auto-creates the game config file (sm64config.txt)
6. Renders the ROM upload UI correctly (verified via screenshot)
7. The Module.onRuntimeInitialized callback fires

The WASM module reaches the point where it expects a ROM file.
The ROM picker UI is displayed and functional. The game cannot
proceed further without a ROM file being selected.

WebGL initialization fails in headless mode (expected - no GPU).
In a real browser, WebGL should work correctly. The
getContextSafariWebGL2Fixed error is specific to the headless
testing environment.

==================================================
KNOWN ISSUES / NEXT STEPS
==================================================

1. WebGL rendering: Untested in real browser (headless has no GPU).
   Need manual browser test to verify GL rendering pipeline.

2. "Invalid or unexpected token" error: Needs source-level debugging
   to identify which EM_ASM or emscripten_run_script call has the
   syntax issue. May need --source-map-base for debugging.

3. FS.syncfs race: Minor - two concurrent IDBFS syncs. Can be fixed
   by ensuring web_storage_init() completes before any other FS.syncfs
   call occurs.

4. ROM loading flow: The file picker is ready but needs manual testing.
   The ASYNCIFY-based polling loop (web_rom_loader.c) needs verification
   with an actual ROM file.

5. Audio: Not yet tested. miniaudio with Web Audio API backend needs
   verification.

6. Input handling: Not yet tested. SDL2 keyboard/gamepad input needs
   browser verification.

7. WASM size: 62MB is very large for a web application. Consider:
   - Enabling -Oz optimization
   - Stripping debug info (-g0)
   - Compressing with Brotli/gzip on the server

